 "description": "Kingston's ultra-secure DataTraveler 5000 USB Flash drive protects sensitive data with FIPS 140-2 Level 2 certification and 256-bit AES hardware-based encryption in XEX mode. Secured by Spyrus, DT5000 uses elliptic curve cryptography encryption algorithms (ECC) that meet the Suite B standards approved by the U.S. government. The drive features complex password protection and locks down after 10 intrusion attempts. DT5000 is waterproof (up to 4 feet) and features a rugged, titanium-coated steel casing.",
